      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT to understand what needs to be improved.Now I have a clear picture. The original test has several understandability issues:\n1. Unused data provider methods (`data_valid`, `data_invalid`) and their imports clutter the class\n2. The boundary value expressions `(Integer.MAX_VALUE / 60) * 60` are unexplained\n3. The assertions lack grouping/comments to convey intent\n\nI'll write an improved version now.Now I'll run the compile check.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored `TestMinutes_test_ofHours.java` removes unused data provider methods and imports, introduces named constants (`MAX_WHOLE_HOURS`, `MIN_WHOLE_HOURS`) to explain the boundary values, and adds inline comments that group assertions by intent — all without changing the called methods, arguments, or expected outcomes."
